<header><p class="enc-kicker">People / group</p><h1 class="enc-title">Kulmiye</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates"><a href="/years/2002">2002</a>–</span> · <a href="/centuries/21st-century">21st century</a> · Also known as Kulmiye Peace, Unity and Development Party</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Kulmiye (Peace, Unity and Development Party) is a political party in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/italian-somaliland">Somaliland</a> founded in 2002 by <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/ahmed-mohamed-mohamoud">Ahmed Mohamed Mohamoud</a> (Silanyo). It won the presidential elections of 2010 and 2017, with Silanyo and then <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/muse-bihi-abdi">Muse Bihi Abdi</a>, and governed until its defeat by the Waddani party in November 2024.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/kulmiye.jpg" alt="Kulmiye" width="320" height="192" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Kulmiye_logo.png" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
